- [nvfp4_scale_layout.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_scale_layout.h#L10), [nvfp4_scale_layout.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_scale_layout.cpp#L54), [device_nvfp4_matrix.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/device_nvfp4_matrix.h#L12), and [device_nvfp4_matrix.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu#L217): added explicit NVFP4 execution-scale layout support and made activation packing auto-select `swizzled_8x4` for small-`M` activations (`M <= 32`), while keeping weight-side swizzling on `swizzled_128x4`.
- [nvfp4_packing.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_packing.h#L12) and [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L127): threaded the chosen activation scale layout through runtime pack options and logged it on fastpath plan/execute failures.
- [nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp#L25), [dense_gemm_runner.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/dense_gemm_runner.cpp#L44), and [cublaslt_gemm_plan.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/loader/cublaslt_gemm_plan.cpp#L18): added exact cuBLASLt/CUDA status logging and concrete plan-reject reasons.
- [device_nvfp4_matrix_test.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/testing/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix_test.cpp#L328): added regression coverage for the small-`M` `8x4` path.
- [PLAN.md](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/proj-2026-04-01-1534/PLAN.md#L342): recorded the checkpoint note.

**Root Cause Analysis**
- The fixed bug was that runtime NVFP4 activation packing always emitted the `128x4` execution-scale swizzle.
- The upstream reference path uses `8x4` for decode-like shapes when `M <= 32`.
- For `M=1`, that means the fastpath could feed cuBLASLt correctly packed FP4 values but incorrectly laid-out activation scale factors.
- Inference from the reference anchors: this is the strongest current explanation for the expert-layer-13 split-prefill divergence. I did not rerun the full real-model parity path in this turn, so I’m not claiming it is the only remaining issue yet.

